# Round w3r5c's decode card: MiMo-V2.6-Flash (MXFP4 experts, Q8_0 dense tier) on plan (a), the A6000 alone, with the hot
# routed experts on the card (R5c: the common MXFP4 pair in the host leg's shadow) against main with every routed expert
# on the host. Decomposition [derived, specs/worker3/r5design/report.md §4], one decode step at n = 1:
# - experts: 13,369,344 B each (3 x 4,096 x 2,048 values x 17/32), 12,032 of them, 160.86 GB. The A6000's room 48,592 MiB
#   less 1,600 MiB (context 512, scratch 64, margin 1,024), the dense 5.84 GB and the KV planes (222,720 B a position at
#   4,160) holds 3,118..3,179 of them (26 %, 66..68 a routed layer; the plan print of gate-mimo2-meta bounds it, the
#   allocator's granules the spread). The card's expert share of a token's 8 slots is 0.26 x 8 = 2.1 slots, the host's
#   k_host = 5.9 (all-host: 8.0).
# - host leg a routed layer: 21..36 us floor + k_host x 92.2..102.8 us (13.37 MB at 130..145 GB/s) = 565..643 us on
#   plan (a), 758..857 us all-host. The card's shadow under it: 6 launches x (0.85 + 1.2..5.8 us) + 2.1 x 13.37 MB at
#   579 GB/s (48.5 us) = 61..89 us a layer, inside the host leg, so worth 0 on the wall.
# - card side, unchanged by R5c: gemv 8.30..9.17 ms, small kernels 1.0..2.4, nodes 0.53, sync 47 x 21..36 us: 10.82..13.79
#   ms; depth adds 0.07..0.20 ms at 1,024 and 0.2..0.6 at 4,096. The step's graph holds 625 + 6 x 47 = 907 nodes
#   (the shadow's six launches on each routed layer; the go and wait pair stays 94).
# - step: all-host 34.7..38.7 ms host + the card side overlapped to 19.0..22.0 tok/s (mid 20.4); plan (a) 25.6..28.5 ms
#   host, 23.6..27.5 tok/s (mid 25.4). Ratio 1.23..1.26. The KV planes without a ring cost 60 experts at 4,160, under
#   0.5 %, inside the ruler.
# - the terms that can miss: the host leg's per-expert time at k_host 5.9 (BW_host, the 21..36 us floor) and the routed
#   mass the id prefix carries (the realized card share of the slots). Both have free reads: the base arm in this lease,
#   and the host tier's card-slot share on any functional run.
# Sitting [worker3's]: the two binaries (main's and this round's) in one lease at the same A6000 and ctx, 4 rounds each,
# load ~41 s warm a process (the 161.6 GB host copy in the page cache), 2 arms x (4 + 1 warm-up) x ~1.5..2 min: 15..20 min.
kind: ab
question: with the hot routed experts of MiMo-V2.6-Flash on the A6000 beside the host tier (R5c), does decode run faster
  than with every routed expert on the host, by the host slots the card takes off the host leg?
term: decode tok/s @ n=64 greedy ids, prose depth 6, ctx 4,160, A6000 alone (the 3090 idle), one stream, R5c's binary
  against main's, paired by round, the runner's per-round ratio (R5c / main) less 1
unit: %
predict: +23..+26
rounds: 4
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」, same-binary paired ratio SD
condition: both binaries in one lease on the A6000, every row's card field A6000 and each witness block with no Xid before
  or after any arm; a fresh process a run with the 161.6 GB host copy resident (majflt ~0, no [cold], [cpu-busy] or
  [other-busy] on a row); the R5c arm's plan record reads card_experts 3,118..3,179 and the base arm's 0, the step's graph
  907 nodes against 625 (gate_mimo2_e2e's structure clause); the full output to a file first
decide-in: the card experts pay as derived: land R5c, publish the depth rows (1,024 and 4,096 positions) and the A6000
  row in the README's MiMo table, and open the tier attach (bp) round
decide-below: below +23 the host leg or the realized share is off the derivation: between +18 and +23 read the base
  arm's host leg per expert and the card's slot share from the plan before landing (the effect is real but the term to
  re-fit is named by them); below +18 BLOOMERY_PROFILE=1 on one arm of each binary for the host leg's times and the
  slots the card took, and hold the landing until the missing term is named
decide-above: above +26 the host leg is slower per expert than 92..103 us (BW_host under 130 GB/s on this file) or the
  prefix carries more than 26 % of the routed mass: re-fit BW_host for MiMo from the base arm's host leg and land
